<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav April industry output falls 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav April industry output falls 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office</p>
<p>reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  APRIL	 MARCH    APRIL 96</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	    - 0.1	 + 7.4	- 3.4</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+ 9.4	 + 9.2	+ 2.5</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)   104.8	 104.5	102.5</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO APRIL)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+ 7.3	 + 6.6	+ 3.3</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1993)   102.1	  99.1	 93.1</p>
<p>NOTES -- April 1997 industry output was 53.1 percent below the the same month in 1991, before former Yugoslavia's breakup.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-April industry output was 55.1 percent below the figure for the same three-month period in 1991.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude private sector, where manufacturing is not significant.</p>
<p>Data cover Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising</p>
<p>Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
